    "reconciliation": "In the CTA-BENCH-002 harness TOPOLOGY-U labels the unified analytical data flow: the visual-to-text stage is the VLM and the VLM-extracted text is fed into the LLM analytical stage, which raises structured-schema validity to 0.941 (bare LLM-MLX-4B/9B fail the hard gate at 0.059/0.176). The accepted full application-path E2E runs two loopback servers: mlx-vlm.server on 127.0.0.1:8091 serves visual extraction (mlx-community/Qwen3-VL-4B-Instruct-4bit) and mlx-openai-server on 127.0.0.1:8093 serves the analytical structured-output stages (mlx-community/Qwen3.5-4B-MLX-4bit). Both processes are resident simultaneously; TOPOLOGY-R co-residency is allowed with headroom_fraction 0.564 (>=0.20), no swap thrashing, graceful shutdown and residual=[] in the artifact, so dual_server_resident does not contradict the TOPOLOGY-U label. Sequential/manual fallback is required only if memory pressure or swap exceeds the frozen envelope, or a server fails exact model identity; the operator then starts the LLM only after the VLM is healthy and stops both before unloading."
